IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part3`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part5`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part6`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part7`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part9`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part10`

-- Interpretation Act 1984 (Western Australia) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has a time limit to meet under a Western Australian Act (to apply, object, appeal, reply or pay), or who
-- needs to know when something takes effect, asking on which day their period ends and which of their days count.
--
-- This layer phrases rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions that person asks.
-- Nothing here is new law, and no layer-1 rule is restated: each question builds the small records the module expects from
-- plain answers, in its WHERE, and calls the module's own rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes yes/no answers, numbers, dates, lists of dates and the modules' own short choices, each with
-- an @desc worded as the person would be asked.  Holidays are two lists of dates, because that is how a person knows them:
-- "the public holidays and bank holidays where I am" and "the public service holidays".  The Act treats every kind of holiday
-- alike (section 61(2) makes each one an excluded day), so which list a date is on makes no difference to any answer.
-- The Act's own days (1 July 1984 and the other fixed figures in the modules) are used as the Act states them.
--
-- NOT COVERED is NOTHING.  A question whose answer is MAYBE says NOTHING when the text does not answer it for the facts given
-- (a period counted in weeks, which the Act does not mention; a case a section does not reach).
--
-- Sections in the text's order.  Every group heading below is a situation the person is already in: a time limit they have to meet,
-- a decision about to be made, a document sent to them.

§ `Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) -- the questions of a person who has a time limit`

§§ `Coming into operation: when does an Act or a provision take effect (ss 20, 21, 25, 27)`

-- s 20.  An Act that names no day of its own comes into operation: if assent was before 1 July 1984, on the day of assent;
-- if on or after 1 July 1984, on the 28th day after the day of assent; if it was reserved on or after 1 July 1984, on the day
-- Her Majesty's assent is proclaimed in the Gazette.  The module decides which; the person states the facts.
@export On which day does an Act come into operation (s 20)?
GIVEN `the Act was reserved for Her Majesty's pleasure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the Act reserved for the signification of Her Majesty's pleasure, instead of receiving Royal Assent straight away?
      `the day of assent, or the day the Act was reserved` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Act receive Royal Assent (or, if it was reserved, on what day was it reserved)?
      `Her Majesty's assent has been proclaimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the Act was reserved, has Her Majesty's assent been proclaimed in the Gazette?
      `the day the assent was proclaimed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the assent proclaimed in the Gazette? (Any date if it has not been)
      `the Act names its own day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act itself name the day it comes into operation?
      `the day the Act names` IS A DATE @desc What day does the Act name? (Any date if it names none)
      `the Act leaves the day to proclamation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act say it comes into operation on a day to be fixed by proclamation?
      `the day fixed by proclamation` IS A DATE @desc What day has the proclamation fixed? (Any date if none has been fixed yet)
      `a proclamation has fixed the day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a proclamation actually fixed the day yet?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does an Act come into operation` IS
    `the day an Act comes into operation` how `the day of assent, or the day the Act was reserved` proclaimed itself
    WHERE
        how MEANS
            IF `the Act was reserved for Her Majesty's pleasure`
            THEN `reserved for the signification of Her Majesty's pleasure`
            ELSE `Royal Assent given`
        proclaimed MEANS
            IF `Her Majesty's assent has been proclaimed` THEN JUST `the day the assent was proclaimed` ELSE NOTHING
        itself MEANS
            IF `the Act names its own day`
            THEN `a particular day` `the day the Act names`
            ELSE
                IF `the Act leaves the day to proclamation`
                THEN `a day to be fixed by proclamation` (IF `a proclamation has fixed the day` THEN JUST `the day fixed by proclamation` ELSE NOTHING)
                ELSE `nothing about it`

-- s 21.  A written law comes into operation at the beginning of its commencement day.
@export Is the law already in operation at a given hour of its first day (s 21)?
GIVEN `the day the law comes into operation` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the law come into operation?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `the hour I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour of that day (0 for midnight, 9 for 9 am, 17 for 5 pm)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the law already in operation at a given hour of its first day` IS
    `a written law is in operation at` moment `given that it comes into operation on` `the day the law comes into operation`
    WHERE
        moment MEANS
            `Moment of a day` WITH
                `the calendar day`  IS `the day I am asking about`
                `second of the day` IS `the hour I am asking about` TIMES 3600

-- s 25(3).  A notice or instrument made early, under a power exercised before the provision commences, takes effect no earlier
-- than the commencement day.
@export On which day does a notice or instrument made before the provision commenced take effect (s 25(3))?
GIVEN `the day the provision commences` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the provision that lets the notice or instrument be made commence?
      `the day it would take effect if the provision had already commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the notice or instrument take effect if the provision had already commenced?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day does a notice or instrument made early take effect` IS
    `the day an instrument or notice made early takes effect` `the day the provision commences` `the day it would take effect if the provision had already commenced`

§§ `Repeal: how long does the old law last (s 35)`

-- Situational: asked only if a provision you rely on is being repealed and replaced.

-- s 35.  Where a law is repealed and replaced, the old provision stays in operation until the new one comes into operation.
@export Is the old provision still in operation on a given day, until its replacement comes in (s 35)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `the day the replacement provisions come into operation` IS A DATE @desc On what day do the replacement provisions come into operation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the old provision still in operation on a given day` IS
    `the repealed enactment remains in operation on` `the day I am asking about` `until the substituted provisions come into operation on` `the day the replacement provisions come into operation`

§§ `Regulations and other subsidiary legislation: when they start, and when they stop (ss 41, 42, 43)`

-- Situational: asked only if regulations, rules, local laws or bylaws affect you.

-- s 41(1)(b).  Subsidiary legislation comes into operation on the day it is published, unless it names another day.
@export On which day do regulations or other subsidiary legislation come into operation (s 41(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the day it was published in the Gazette or on the WA legislation website` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it published in the Gazette or on the WA legislation website?
      `it names another day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the legislation itself name, or provide for, another day for it to come into operation?
      `the other day it names` IS A DATE @desc What day does it name? (Any date if it names none)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day does subsidiary legislation come into operation` IS
    `the day subsidiary legislation comes into operation` `the day it was published in the Gazette or on the WA legislation website` other
    WHERE
        other MEANS IF `it names another day` THEN JUST `the other day it names` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 42(2).  Regulations cease to have effect if a House passes a resolution disallowing them (notice given within 14 sitting days
-- after they were laid before it), or if they were not laid before both Houses as required.
@export Have the regulations that affect me ceased to have effect (s 42(2))?
GIVEN `a House passed a resolution disallowing them, after notice given within 14 sitting days of its being laid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a House of Parliament passed a resolution disallowing the regulations, on notice given within 14 sitting days after they were laid before it?
      `they were not laid before both Houses as required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the regulations not laid before both Houses of Parliament within 6 sitting days of each House after publication?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have the regulations that affect me ceased to have effect` IS
    `the regulations cease to have effect` `a House passed a resolution disallowing them, after notice given within 14 sitting days of its being laid` `they were not laid before both Houses as required`

-- s 42(4).  Regulations amended or substituted by a resolution of both Houses take effect after the expiration of 7 days from the
-- publication of the notice of the resolution.
@export On which day do the amended or substituted regulations take effect (s 42(4))?
GIVEN `the day the notice of the resolution was published` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice of the resolution published in the Gazette or on the WA legislation website?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day do the amended or substituted regulations take effect` IS
    `the first day the amended or substituted regulations take effect` `the day the notice of the resolution was published`

-- s 42(6).  Where regulations that amended or repealed earlier ones are disallowed, or were not laid, the earlier ones are revived.
@export On which day are the earlier regulations revived (s 42(6))?
GIVEN `the regulations were disallowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the regulations disallowed by a resolution of a House (answer no if instead they were not laid as required)?
      `the regulations amended or repealed regulations that were in operation just before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the regulations amend or repeal regulations that were in operation immediately before they came into operation?
      `the day of the disallowance` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the regulations disallowed? (Any date if they were not)
      `the last day for laying them` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day for laying them before Parliament? (Any date if they were disallowed)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day are the earlier regulations revived` IS
    `the first day the previous regulations are revived` how `the regulations amended or repealed regulations that were in operation just before` `the day of the disallowance` `the last day for laying them`
    WHERE
        how MEANS
            IF `the regulations were disallowed`
            THEN `disallowed by a resolution`
            ELSE `not laid in accordance with subsection (1)`

-- s 43(6).  The most a regulation, rule, local law or bylaw may fine: $1000, for a power conferred by an enactment passed or made on
-- or after 1 July 1984 (and not one that merely continues or directly amends existing text).
@export What is the most I can be fined under a regulation, rule, local law or bylaw (s 43(6))?
GIVEN `the day the enactment giving the power to make it was passed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the Act or other enactment that gives the power to make the regulation, rule, local law or bylaw passed or made?
      `that enactment only continues or directly amends existing text` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that enactment only continue, or directly amend, the text of an earlier written law (without repealing it entirely)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined under a regulation, rule, local law or bylaw` IS
    `the most a fine may be under regulations, rules, local laws or bylaws` `the day the enactment giving the power to make it was passed` `that enactment only continues or directly amends existing text`

§§ `Decisions that affect me: who may make them and when they stand (ss 48A, 49, 51, 54, 57)`

-- s 48A.  A power to act judicially, serve a document or court process, or execute a warrant may be exercised on any day, even a
-- Saturday, Sunday or public holiday.
@export May a court document be served on me, or a warrant executed, on a weekend or public holiday (s 48A)?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `it is a power to act judicially, serve a document or court process, or execute a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a power to act judicially, to serve a document or court process, or to execute a warrant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a court document be served on me on a weekend or public holiday` IS
    `the power may be exercised on` `the day I am asking about` `if` `it is a power to act judicially, serve a document or court process, or execute a warrant`

-- s 49.  A power given to the holder of a public office may be exercised by the person for the time being holding, acting in or
-- performing the functions of the office.
@export Can a person who is only acting in the office make the decision that affects me (s 49)?
GIVEN who IS A `Who is asked about under section 49` @desc Is the person making the decision the one lawfully holding the office, someone acting in it, or someone performing its functions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a person who is only acting in the office make the decision` IS
    `the person may exercise the power and must perform the duty of the public office` who

-- s 51(1).  A person with power to issue or renew a licence, permit or other authorisation has a discretion to grant or to refuse.
@export Is the authority free to refuse my application for a licence or permit (s 51(1))?
GIVEN `the law lets the authority issue, grant, give or renew it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written law give the authority power to issue, grant, give or renew the licence, registration, lease, right, authority, approval, permit or exemption?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the authority free to refuse my application` IS
    `the person empowered has a discretion to grant or to refuse` `the law lets the authority issue, grant, give or renew it`

-- s 51(2).  A right a written law gives to appeal, apply, or seek review of a refusal is left in place.
@export Can I still appeal against or seek a review of a refusal (s 51(2))?
GIVEN `a written law gives me a right to appeal, apply or seek review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written law give you a right to appeal against, apply for, or seek a review of the refusal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still appeal against or seek a review of a refusal` IS
    `the right to appeal against or seek review of a refusal is left in place` `a written law gives me a right to appeal, apply or seek review`

-- s 54(2)(b).  An act done by a majority of the members present at a meeting is the association's act, if those present are a quorum.
-- The quorum for a body with a fixed number of members (3 or more) is s 54(2)(a)(i): at least one half of that number.  For any
-- other body the section does not say what the quorum is, and the answer is NOTHING.
@export Was the board's decision validly made by the members at the meeting (s 54(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the number of members present` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members were at the meeting?
      `the number of members present who agreed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those present agreed to the decision?
      `the number of members the law provides for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members does the law that set up the board provide for (a fixed number of 3 or more)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the board's decision validly made by the members at the meeting` IS
    CONSIDER `the least number of members that make a quorum, with a fixed number of members` `the number of members the law provides for`
    WHEN JUST quorum THEN JUST (`the act is deemed done by the association` `the number of members present` `the number of members present who agreed` quorum)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 57.  The powers of a board, tribunal, commission, committee or council are not affected by a vacancy, a defect in a member's
-- appointment, a minor irregularity in a meeting, or the presence of a person not entitled to be there.
@export Is the decision of the body invalid because of a vacancy or an irregularity (s 57)?
GIVEN defect IS A `Defect in a statutory body` @desc What went wrong: a vacancy, a defect in a member's appointment, a minor irregularity, someone present who should not have been, or a major irregularity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the decision of the body invalid because of a vacancy or an irregularity` IS
    `the powers of the body are affected by` defect

§§ `Counting my time (ss 61, 62, 63, 64)`

-- Shared: the Act counts a Saturday, a Sunday and each kind of holiday as an excluded day (s 61(2)).  A person lists the dates.
GIVEN `public holidays and bank holidays where I am` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `public service holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A `Holidays that make an excluded day`
`my holidays, as the Act counts them` `public holidays and bank holidays where I am` `public service holidays` MEANS
    `Holidays that make an excluded day` WITH
        `public service holidays`            IS `public service holidays`
        `bank holidays in the relevant area`   IS EMPTY
        `public holidays in the relevant area` IS `public holidays and bank holidays where I am`

-- ss 61(1)(a), (b), (d), (e), 62.  The last day I have to do the thing, once the calendar and then weekends and holidays are
-- counted: a period runs from or after a day (the day itself does not count) or begins at, on or with it (it does); a month is a
-- calendar month; an end that falls on an excluded day moves to the next day that is not one.
@export What is the last day I have to do it (ss 61, 62)?
GIVEN `the length of my period` IS A NUMBER @desc How long is your period? Give the number only (28 for 28 days, 3 for 3 months).
      `the unit my period is counted in` IS A `Unit of a period` @desc Is the period counted in days, weeks, months or years?
      `how my period is tied to the day` IS A `How a period is tied to a day` @desc Does the law say the period begins at, on or with the day, or runs from or after it? ("within 28 days after the decision" runs from or after it.)
      `the day named in the law` IS A DATE @desc What is the day the law names: the day of the decision, the notice, the service or the offence?
      `public holidays and bank holidays where I am` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List the public holidays and bank holidays, where you are, that fall on or near the end of your period.
      `public service holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List any public service holidays that fall on or near the end of your period.
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day I have to do it` IS
    CONSIDER `reckon a period` period `how my period is tied to the day` `the day named in the law` (`my holidays, as the Act counts them` `public holidays and bank holidays where I am` `public service holidays`)
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (r's `end`'s `last day for doing the thing`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        period MEANS `Period of time` WITH `number of units` IS `the length of my period`, `unit` IS `the unit my period is counted in`

-- The same period before any move for a weekend or holiday: the date the calendar gives.
@export What is the last day of my period by the calendar, before a weekend or holiday moves it (ss 61, 62)?
GIVEN `the length of my period` IS A NUMBER @desc How long is your period? Give the number only (28 for 28 days, 3 for 3 months).
      `the unit my period is counted in` IS A `Unit of a period` @desc Is the period counted in days, weeks, months or years?
      `how my period is tied to the day` IS A `How a period is tied to a day` @desc Does the law say the period begins at, on or with the day, or runs from or after it?
      `the day named in the law` IS A DATE @desc What is the day the law names: the day of the decision, the notice, the service or the offence?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day of my period by the calendar` IS
    CONSIDER `reckon a period` period `how my period is tied to the day` `the day named in the law` (`my holidays, as the Act counts them` EMPTY EMPTY)
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (r's `end`'s `last day by the calendar`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        period MEANS `Period of time` WITH `number of units` IS `the length of my period`, `unit` IS `the unit my period is counted in`

@export What is the first day that counts in my period (ss 61(1)(a), 61(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the length of my period` IS A NUMBER @desc How long is your period? Give the number only (28 for 28 days, 3 for 3 months).
      `the unit my period is counted in` IS A `Unit of a period` @desc Is the period counted in days, weeks, months or years?
      `how my period is tied to the day` IS A `How a period is tied to a day` @desc Does the law say the period begins at, on or with the day, or runs from or after it?
      `the day named in the law` IS A DATE @desc What is the day the law names?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `What is the first day that counts in my period` IS
    CONSIDER `reckon a period` period `how my period is tied to the day` `the day named in the law` (`my holidays, as the Act counts them` EMPTY EMPTY)
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (r's `first day`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        period MEANS `Period of time` WITH `number of units` IS `the length of my period`, `unit` IS `the unit my period is counted in`

-- s 61(1)(e), (h).  Am I in time if I act on a given day?
@export Am I in time if I do it on a given day (ss 61, 62)?
GIVEN `the day I plan to do it` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you plan to do it (file, pay, reply or appeal)?
      `the length of my period` IS A NUMBER @desc How long is your period? Give the number only (28 for 28 days, 3 for 3 months).
      `the unit my period is counted in` IS A `Unit of a period` @desc Is the period counted in days, weeks, months or years?
      `how my period is tied to the day` IS A `How a period is tied to a day` @desc Does the law say the period begins at, on or with the day, or runs from or after it?
      `the day named in the law` IS A DATE @desc What is the day the law names?
      `public holidays and bank holidays where I am` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List the public holidays and bank holidays, where you are, that fall on or near the end of your period.
      `public service holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List any public service holidays that fall on or near the end of your period.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I in time if I do it on a given day` IS
    CONSIDER `reckon a period` period `how my period is tied to the day` `the day named in the law` (`my holidays, as the Act counts them` `public holidays and bank holidays where I am` `public service holidays`)
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (Day `the day I plan to do it` AT MOST Day (r's `end`'s `last day for doing the thing`))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        period MEANS `Period of time` WITH `number of units` IS `the length of my period`, `unit` IS `the unit my period is counted in`

-- s 61(2).  Which of my days count?
@export Is this day an excluded day: a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday (s 61(2))?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `public holidays and bank holidays where I am` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List the public holidays and bank holidays, where you are, that you know of near that day.
      `public service holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List any public service holidays near that day.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this day an excluded day` IS
    `is an excluded day` `the day I am asking about` (`my holidays, as the Act counts them` `public holidays and bank holidays where I am` `public service holidays`)

-- s 61(1)(e), (h).  The day set for me is an excluded day: I am in due time if I act on the next day that is not one.
@export The day set for me to act is an excluded day: what is the latest day I can act and still be in time (ss 61(1)(e), 61(1)(h))?
GIVEN `the day set for me` IS A DATE @desc What is the day the law or the notice sets for you to act?
      `public holidays and bank holidays where I am` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List the public holidays and bank holidays, where you are, that fall on or near that day.
      `public service holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List any public service holidays that fall on or near that day.
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `The day set for me is an excluded day: the latest day I can act` IS
    `the next day that is not an excluded day, counting the day itself` `the day set for me` (`my holidays, as the Act counts them` `public holidays and bank holidays where I am` `public service holidays`)

-- s 61(1)(c).  "Within 7 days before the hearing": the time does not include the day named.
@export What is the last day I can act if I must do it within a number of days before a day (s 61(1)(c))?
GIVEN `the number of days` IS A NUMBER @desc Within how many days before the day must you act?
      `the day named in the law` IS A DATE @desc What is the day named (the hearing, the meeting, the closing date)?
      `public holidays and bank holidays where I am` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List the public holidays and bank holidays, where you are, that fall on or near the end of that time.
      `public service holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List any public service holidays that fall on or near the end of that time.
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day I can act if I must do it within a number of days before a day` IS
    CONSIDER `the time within a time before a day` period `the day named in the law` (`my holidays, as the Act counts them` `public holidays and bank holidays where I am` `public service holidays`)
    WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (r's `end`'s `last day for doing the thing`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        period MEANS `Period of time` WITH `number of units` IS `the number of days`, `unit` IS `in days`

-- s 61(1)(f), (g).  The number of days between two events.
@export How many days are there between the two events (ss 61(1)(f), 61(1)(g))?
GIVEN `how the law expresses the number of days` IS A `How a count of days between two events is expressed` @desc Does the law say "clear days", "at least" or "not less than" a number of days, or just a number of days?
      `the day the first event happens` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the first event happen (for example, the notice is given)?
      `the day the second event happens` IS A DATE @desc On what day does the second event happen (for example, the hearing)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days are there between the two events` IS
    `the number of days counted between two events` `how the law expresses the number of days` `the day the first event happens` `the day the second event happens`

-- s 63.  No time is fixed: do it with all convenient speed, and as often as occasion arises.
@export If the law fixes no time for me to act, must I act with all convenient speed (s 63)?
GIVEN `the law fixes or allows a time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law fix or allow a time within which you must do it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `If the law fixes no time must I act with all convenient speed` IS
    `the act or thing must be done with all convenient speed and as often as occasion arises` `the law fixes or allows a time`

-- s 64.  A power to extend a time may be used after the time has run out.
@export May I ask for more time after my time has run out (s 64)?
GIVEN `a court or authority has power to extend the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law give a court or other authority power to extend the time?
      `the day the law giving that power was passed or made` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the law that gives that power passed or made?
      `that law only continues or directly amends existing text` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that law only continue, or directly amend, the text of an earlier written law (without repealing it entirely)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask for more time after my time has run out` IS
    `an application to extend may be made after the time has expired` `a court or authority has power to extend the time` `the day the law giving that power was passed or made` `that law only continues or directly amends existing text`

§§ `If I do not do it: continuing offences (s 71)`

-- Situational: asked only if you have been convicted of failing to do something the law required and you still have not done it.

-- s 71(1)(e), 71(2).  After a conviction for failing to do something, each further day of failure is a separate and further offence.
@export How many further offences am I guilty of if I still have not done it (s 71)?
GIVEN `the day I was convicted` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you convicted of failing to do it?
      `the last day I have still not done it` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day, so far, on which you have still not done it?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many further offences am I guilty of` IS
    `the number of separate and further offences` `the day I was convicted` `the last day I have still not done it`

-- s 71(1)(f).  Unless the law says otherwise, each further offence carries a penalty of $50.
@export How much is the penalty for each further offence (s 71(1)(f))?
GIVEN `the law sets a different penalty for each further offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law that required you to act set a different penalty for each further offence?
      `that penalty in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is that penalty, in dollars? (Any number if it sets none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the penalty for each further offence` IS
    `the penalty for each separate and further offence` provided
    WHERE
        provided MEANS IF `the law sets a different penalty for each further offence` THEN JUST `that penalty in dollars` ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Forms and documents sent to me or by me (ss 74, 75, 76)`

-- s 74.  A deviation from a prescribed form that neither materially affects the substance nor is likely to mislead does not
-- invalidate the form used.
@export Does a small mistake in the prescribed form I used make it invalid (s 74)?
GIVEN `the mistake materially affects the substance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the mistake materially affect the substance of the form?
      `the mistake is likely to mislead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the mistake likely to mislead the person reading it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a small mistake in the prescribed form I used make it invalid` IS
    `the deviation invalidates the form used` `the mistake materially affects the substance` `the mistake is likely to mislead`

-- s 75(1).  A document posted is taken to be served when the letter would have been delivered in the ordinary course of post,
-- unless the contrary is proved.
@export On which day is a document sent by post taken to be served (s 75(1))?
GIVEN `it was properly addressed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the letter properly addressed?
      `it was posted by prepaid post` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it posted by prepaid post?
      `it was posted as a letter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it posted as a letter?
      `it went to the last known address of the person to be served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it addressed to the last known address of the person to be served?
      `the day it would have been delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the letter have been delivered in the ordinary course of post?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can it be proved that it was delivered on a different day?
      `the day it was in fact delivered` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it in fact delivered? (Any date if that cannot be proved)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day is a document sent by post taken to be served` IS
    `the day service by post is deemed effected` `it was properly addressed` `it was posted by prepaid post` `it was posted as a letter` `it went to the last known address of the person to be served` `the day it would have been delivered in the ordinary course of post` actual
    WHERE
        actual MEANS IF `the contrary is proved` THEN JUST `the day it was in fact delivered` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 75(2), (3).  A document to be served by registered post may also be served by certified mail, if it is eligible and acceptable.
@export May a document that must be served by registered post be sent by certified mail instead (ss 75(2), 75(3))?
GIVEN `the law requires service by registered post` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written law authorise or require the document to be served by registered post?
      `the document is eligible and acceptable for certified mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document eligible and acceptable for transmission as certified mail?
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law show a contrary intention?
      `the law requires a signed acknowledgment of delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law require production of an acknowledgment, signed by the person the document was addressed to, that it was delivered to them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a document that must be served by registered post be sent by certified mail instead` IS
    `service may be effected either by registered post or by certified mail` `the law requires service by registered post` `the document is eligible and acceptable for certified mail` `a contrary intention appears` `the law requires a signed acknowledgment of delivery`

-- s 76.  Service where the law directs no particular manner: personally, by post, by leaving it at the usual or last known place of
-- abode (or business of a principal of a business), or, for a corporation or association, at its principal place of business.
@export May a document be served on me in this way (s 76)?
GIVEN manner IS A `Manner of serving a document` @desc How is the document being served on you: handed to you, posted, left at your home, left at your business, left at a corporation's or association's principal place of business, or some other way?
      `the law directs a particular manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law that requires the document to be served direct a particular manner of service?
      `I am a principal of a business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a principal of a business?
      `I am a corporation or an association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a corporation or an association of persons, incorporated or not?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a document be served on me in this way` IS
    `service may be effected in the manner` manner `the law directs a particular manner` `I am a principal of a business` `I am a corporation or an association`

§§ `Old Acts (passed before 1 July 1984) that adopt the Second Schedule of the 1918 Act (s 77(4))`

-- Situational: asked only if the Act you are charged under was passed before 1 July 1984 and adopts a section of the 1918 Act's Second Schedule.

-- s 77(4) and the 1918 Act's Second Schedule, sections B to E.  How long after an offence the complaint may be made.
@export By which day must the complaint be made and the proceedings started (s 77(4), Second Schedule B to E of the 1918 Act)?
GIVEN section IS A `Section of the Second Schedule that fixes a time to complain` @desc Which section of the Second Schedule does the Act use: B (one month), C (three months), D (six months) or E (twelve months)?
      `the day the offence was committed` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the offence committed?
      `public holidays and bank holidays where I am` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List the public holidays and bank holidays, where you are, that fall on or near the end of the time.
      `public service holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc List any public service holidays that fall on or near the end of the time.
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By which day must the complaint be made and the proceedings started` IS
    `the last day to make the complaint and commence the proceedings` section `the day the offence was committed` (`my holidays, as the Act counts them` `public holidays and bank holidays where I am` `public service holidays`)
